; A transaction that exchanges two commodities, without stating a cost or
; leaving a posting blank, gets an inferred price, and Ledger normally
; takes the commodity of its first posting as the one bought, priced in
; the other.  When the first posting holds neither commodity -- a zero fee
; in a third commodity, or balanced virtual budget lines -- the choice
; falls to the commodity that entered the transaction's balance first.
; Ledger adds up the real postings in order, and at the first posting in
; a second commodity the sum of the postings before it enters the balance
; first, unless it is zero: a zero sum never enters, and the first to
; enter is then the commodity of the first non-zero posting from there on.
; In the first transaction that sum is the zero fee, so the 100 GBP
; enters first; in the second the budget lines are not real postings, and
; the sum is the 100 GBP itself.  GBP is bought in both, so the lots go on
; Assets:GBP and the inferred prices are GBP in $ and in EUR.  Picking the
; other commodity would put lots of $ and of EUR, priced in GBP, on
; Assets:USD and Assets:EUR.  The choice must not depend on the order in
; which a balance happens to keep its two commodities, which changes from
; run to run.  Real postings that cancel out before the second commodity
; arrives are the subject of xact-price-inference-cancel-first.test.

2024/01/05 Exchange with a zero fee first
    Assets:Fee              0 EUR
    Assets:GBP            100 GBP
    Assets:USD           $-130

2024/02/05 Exchange after budget lines
    [Budget:Travel]       $100
    [Budget:Available]   $-100
    Assets:GBP            100 GBP
    Assets:EUR           -115 EUR

test bal --lots --flat --no-total Assets
            -115 EUR  Assets:EUR
    100 GBP {$1.3} [2024/01/05]
100 GBP {1.15 EUR} [2024/02/05]  Assets:GBP
               $-130  Assets:USD
end test

test prices
2024/01/05 GBP              $1.3
2024/02/05 GBP          1.15 EUR
end test
